  "content": {
    "id": "p33-q2-root",
    "type": "question",
    "label": "2",
    "prompt": "Suppose $p$, $q$ and $r$ are the roots of the polynomial $x^3-2x^2-14x+24$. Determine the values of:",
    "layout": "grid",
    "columns": 2,
    "questionDiagrams": [],
    "children": [
      {
        "id": "p33-q2-a",
        "type": "part",
        "label": "a",
        "prompt": "$p+q+r$",
        "layout": "list",
        "columns": null,
        "questionDiagrams": [],
        "children": [],
        "answer": {
          "short": "$2$",
          "worked": "By Vieta’s formulas,\n$$\\begin{align*}p+q+r&=-\\frac{-2}{1}\\\\p+q+r&=2.\\end{align*}$$",
          "solutionDiagrams": []
        },
        "answerSpaceMm": 12
      },
      {
        "id": "p33-q2-b",
        "type": "part",
        "label": "b",
        "prompt": "$pqr$",
        "layout": "list",
        "columns": null,
        "questionDiagrams": [],
        "children": [],
        "answer": {
          "short": "$-24$",
          "worked": "By Vieta’s formulas,\n$$\\begin{align*}pqr&=-\\frac{24}{1}\\\\pqr&=-24.\\end{align*}$$",
          "solutionDiagrams": []
        },
        "answerSpaceMm": 12
      },
      {
        "id": "p33-q2-c",
        "type": "part",
        "label": "c",
        "prompt": "$pq+pr+rq$",
        "layout": "list",
        "columns": null,
        "questionDiagrams": [],
        "children": [],
        "answer": {
          "short": "$-14$",
          "worked": "By Vieta’s formulas,\n$$\\begin{align*}pq+pr+rq&=\\frac{-14}{1}\\\\pq+pr+rq&=-14.\\end{align*}$$",
          "solutionDiagrams": []
        },
        "answerSpaceMm": 12
      },
      {
        "id": "p33-q2-d",
        "type": "part",
        "label": "d",
        "prompt": "$\\dfrac1p+\\dfrac1q+\\dfrac1r$",
        "layout": "list",
        "columns": null,
        "questionDiagrams": [],
        "children": [],
        "answer": {
          "short": "$\\dfrac7{12}$",
          "worked": "$$\\begin{align*}\\frac1p+\\frac1q+\\frac1r&=\\frac{qr+pr+pq}{pqr}\\\\\\frac1p+\\frac1q+\\frac1r&=\\frac{-14}{-24}\\\\\\frac1p+\\frac1q+\\frac1r&=\\frac7{12}.\\end{align*}$$",
          "solutionDiagrams": []
        },
        "answerSpaceMm": 30
      },
      {
        "id": "p33-q2-e",
        "type": "part",
        "label": "e",
        "prompt": "$\\dfrac{p}{qr}+\\dfrac{q}{pr}+\\dfrac{r}{pq}$",
        "layout": "list",
        "columns": null,
        "questionDiagrams": [],
        "children": [],
        "answer": {
          "short": "$-\\dfrac43$\n\nUse $p^2+q^2+r^2=(p+q+r)^2-2(pq+pr+qr)$, then divide by $pqr$.",
          "worked": "Using the squared-sum identity,\n$$\\begin{align*}p^2+q^2+r^2&=(p+q+r)^2-2(pq+pr+qr)\\\\p^2+q^2+r^2&=2^2-2(-14)\\\\p^2+q^2+r^2&=32.\\end{align*}$$\nHence,\n$$\\begin{align*}\\frac{p}{qr}+\\frac{q}{pr}+\\frac{r}{pq}&=\\frac{p^2+q^2+r^2}{pqr}\\\\\\frac{p}{qr}+\\frac{q}{pr}+\\frac{r}{pq}&=\\frac{32}{-24}\\\\\\frac{p}{qr}+\\frac{q}{pr}+\\frac{r}{pq}&=-\\frac43.\\end{align*}$$",
          "solutionDiagrams": []
        },
        "answerSpaceMm": 40
      }
    ]
  },
